01:00:58.740 --> 01:00:59.880
Not kind.

01:01:00.510 --> 01:01:14.230
good like senor jean but i i've learned now i've learned mucho from my capitan so i give you a

01:01:14.230 --> 01:01:23.860
chance go for your guns

01:01:53.930 --> 01:01:58.510
She's alright now. Always out.

01:02:00.160 --> 01:02:16.500
I pray to Santa Guadalupe that someday you'll find a lady who'll make you good.

01:02:19.120 --> 01:02:23.670
So I'm pretty happy now.

01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:29.100
Adios.

01:02:30.600 --> 01:02:31.420
It's in your team.

01:02:36.620 --> 01:02:40.840
Dios, por Dios.

01:02:59.450 --> 01:02:59.970
I'm going to leave you.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.470
Here, dear, you're going to be a brave girl.

01:03:03.270 --> 01:03:03.950
Keep your chin up.

01:03:05.330 --> 01:03:05.710
I don't know.

01:03:05.750 --> 01:03:09.900
I don't know if anyone can be brave when the time of parting comes.

01:03:12.270 --> 01:03:12.910
I love you, Jean.

01:03:14.370 --> 01:03:15.230
Afraid to let you go.

01:03:16.360 --> 01:03:17.900
The things I've done must be explained.

01:03:18.980 --> 01:03:22.380
That's why I'm riding south, even if it's a jail sentence.

01:03:24.520 --> 01:03:27.240
Don't throw away love and happiness for something you've done in the past.

01:03:27.620 --> 01:03:29.380
It's our future that counts, that's all.

01:03:31.720 --> 01:03:38.940
Our future is here on the border, and it must start with a clean slate, not with me as a fugitive.

01:03:41.760 --> 01:03:42.960
Surely you understand that?

01:03:47.740 --> 01:03:48.420
Yes, I do.

01:03:50.260 --> 01:03:50.800
Faith, dear.
